Priya Shah: FYI I'm opening a PR to add localization + region availability clarifications. Need a Rust SDK snippet (we don't have that in other threads) and a short Canada (ca-central-1) example. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/501
Omar Vasquez: Also add explicit alias guidance: eu.api.redwood.ai vs api.redwood.ai and note private deployments can have custom hostnames.
Liz Chen: Suggest wording change: 'Hosted regional endpoints process and store data in the selected region for standard accounts. Contractual residency requires agreement.' Add DPA link: https://redwood.ai/compliance/dpa
Priya Shah: Rust snippet added:
```rust
use redwood::Client;

#[tokio::main] async fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
  let mut client = Client::new(std::env::var("RW_KEY")?);
  client = client.with_region("ca-central-1");
  let res = client.generate("redwood-7b", "Summarize: Q2 goals").await?;
  println!("{}", res.text);
  Ok(())
}
```
Omar Vasquez: Nice. Add migration curl one-liner: `curl -X POST https://ca.api.redwood.ai/v1/generate -H 'Authorization: Bearer $RW_KEY' -d '{"model":"redwood-7b","input":"hi"}'`
Liz Chen: docs-ci: please run link-check and swap external map for internal /assets/region-matrix-v3.png
docs-ci: link-check ok. One external vendor map removed. Replaced with /assets/region-matrix-v3.png
legal-bot: include DPA link and advise to avoid absolute claims. Recommend: 'Hosted regional endpoints process and store data in the selected region for standard accounts; custom residency requires contract. Contact legal@redwood.ai.'
Priya Shah: Added availability table: ca-central-1 (preview), eu-west-1 (GA), sa-east-1 (coming soon). Also added note about rate-limits per region and cache warm-up (expect cold misses after migration).
Omar Vasquez: LGTM pending legal sign-off. I'll merge after that. Thanks!
